# A shebang combined with CRLF line endings breaks Vite's ES-module
# transform. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so a Windows
# checkout has CRLF in the working tree, and the stray `\r` left on the
# shebang line becomes a syntax error the moment a test imports the module:
#
#   SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token
#
# Node's own loader copes with a CRLF shebang — it strips the whole line —
# and so does a `require()` of a CommonJS file. Vite's ESM transform does
# not, so the failure only appears in the test suite and not when the
# script is run.
#
# `scripts/ci/validate-slo.mjs` is the one ES module in the repository that
# carries a shebang AND is imported by a test
# (`tests/unit/slo-gate.test.js` imports it to exercise `evaluate()`).
# Keep its line endings as they are committed.
scripts/ci/validate-slo.mjs text eol=lf
